==============================================================================
THE ONE KNOB THAT MOVED IT, AND THE CHEAP METRIC WOULD HAVE TURNED IT TOO FAR
scored 2026-08-22 by tools/probe_bisect.py --paired --json, one pass per
checkpoint per set, all three in the plain basis.

Every checkpoint in this project has been trained at --infonce 0.3. It was
inherited from the first distillation script and never measured. These are
the two neighbouring points, 30 000 images and 20 epochs, everything else
held identical (batch 512, lr 0.006, rkd 0, text 0, same target file):

run              nce      book   glass  laptop  refrig    oven  toilet  umbrel  suitca    bowl     bed    mean
so400m-s30k-nce00 0.0    0.608   0.522   0.393   0.639   0.471   0.430   0.325   0.556   0.658   0.560   0.516
so400m-s30k       0.3    0.565   0.600   0.616   0.714   0.604   0.435   0.421   0.646   0.742   0.618   0.596
so400m-s30k-nce10 1.0    0.577   0.562   0.577   0.698   0.537   0.427   0.446   0.628   0.779   0.587   0.582

teacher 1152             0.907   0.933   0.781   0.786   0.850   0.579   0.715   0.894   0.819   0.847   0.811
pca 512 (plain)          0.917   0.933   0.775   0.804   0.873   0.595   0.725   0.888   0.866   0.872   0.825

Paired differences over the ten sets:
  0.0 -> 0.3 : +0.080 +-0.022
  0.3 -> 1.0 : -0.014 +-0.010
  0.0 -> 1.0 : +0.066 +-0.020

+0.080 is the largest effect any training knob has produced on this eval.
For scale, in the same units and on the same ten sets: six distillation
losses moved the mean by nothing, doubling the schedule moved it by nothing
(-0.011 +-0.026), and quadrupling the training data bought +0.051 +-0.020.
Turning the InfoNCE term on is worth more than 4x the images.

0.0 is worse on nine of the ten sets and the exception is book, +0.043. The
loss is spread rather than carried by one row: laptop -0.223, oven -0.133,
umbrella -0.096, suitcase -0.090, bowl -0.084, glass -0.078, refrigerator
-0.075, bed -0.058, and toilet -0.005, which is toilet doing what toilet
always does. Without the contrastive term the student regresses onto teacher
vectors and keeps the cone without keeping the directions inside it.

AND NOW THE PART WORTH THE FILE
-------------------------------
Holdout top-1, the number model/distill.py prints every epoch:

  infonce   holdout top-1    ten contrasts
     0.0        0.126            0.516
     0.3        0.375            0.596
     1.0        0.434            0.582

Top-1 climbs monotonically and by a lot: 0.126 to 0.434 is a factor of 3.4.
The product metric peaks in the middle and comes back down. A search run on
the cheap number picks 1.0 and ships a checkpoint 0.014 worse, having watched
its headline figure improve by +0.059 on the way.

This is the third time these two have disagreed - see the 20-vs-40-epoch pair
in 20260822-epochs-10contrast.log, where top-1 went +0.054 while the
contrasts went -0.011 - and it is the clearest, because here the cheap metric
is not merely insensitive but confidently wrong about the direction.

The reason is not mysterious. InfoNCE is a retrieval objective and holdout
top-1 is a retrieval measurement, so raising the weight buys the metric
directly. Pooled cross-scene AUC asks a different question: tell this object
state from that one, in a room you have not seen. Retrieval and discrimination
want different amounts of the same term.

So 0.3 was right, by inheritance rather than by measurement, and it is right
by a margin small enough (-0.014 +-0.010 against 1.0) that nobody would have
noticed it being wrong. Leave it there. It is not a fifth constant and there
is no schedule to tune around it - two neighbouring points is what was
measured and two is what may be claimed.

REPRODUCING
-----------
model/runs/ is gitignored, so the commands are here.

  for nce in 0.0 1.0; do
    n=$(echo $nce | tr -d .); n=${n:0:2}
    uv run model/distill.py --split train2017 --epochs 20 \
        --batch 512 --lr 0.006 --infonce $nce --subset 30000 \
        --targets model/cache/emb_train2017_SO400M-pca512_s30000.npy \
        --name so400m-s30k-nce$n
  done

  for r in so400m-s30k-nce00 so400m-s30k-nce10; do
    for s in book glass laptop refrigerator oven toilet umbrella suitcase bowl bed; do
      d=20260822-synth-$s-crop; q=bench/stills/$d/queries.txt
      uv run --script tools/probe_bisect.py \
         --a bench/stills/$d/pos --b bench/stills/$d/neg \
         --pos "$(sed -n 1p $q)" --neg "$(sed -n 2p $q)" \
         --paired --keep bench/stills/$d/keep.txt --runs $r \
         --json model/runs/_full_score_${r}_$s.json
    done
  done

The 0.3 row is so400m-s30k, read from model/runs/_text_score_select_*.json,
which scored it alongside the text sieve on these same sets. All three share
one target file, so the teacher and pca rows are one set of numbers for all
three and the comparison never crosses a space.

The two -a05 checkpoints are NOT in this table. They live in a differently
whitened basis and belong to their own log.
